      "side": 1,
      "message": "You\u0027re right — this check is not needed.\n\nFor single-grapheme clusters (both precomposed 1-glyph and decomposed multi-glyph like `abc+grave`), combining marks lack `kGraphemeStart`, so `graphemes \u003c\u003d 1` already evaluates to true.\n\nThe early return was an artifact from testing decomposed multi-glyph clusters before the grapheme count loop was in place. Keeping it only affects multi-grapheme clusters with multiple glyphs, where we actually want to fall through to proportional clipping (`sizeToChar` / `sizeFromChar`) rather than isolate glyphs.\n\nRemoved in PS 18.",
